 "id": "win98",
 "label": "Windows 98",
 "about": "The 1998 desktop, light only. A window: the page is its frame, the header its title bar (navy to blue, dithered for RGB565, white bold title, minimize / maximize / close drawn as caption buttons), running to the window's edges; cards are small windows with the same title bar. #C0C0C0 face and the four-shade bevel (white / #DFDFDF light, #808080 / black shadow) on tiles and buttons (the primary Button too): pressed = sunken with the dotted focus rectangle, on = latched (sunken on the white-grey checker). Rows are etched, a pressed row is the navy selection. The Segmented is a row of toolbar toggle buttons (the chosen one pressed in, #DFDFDF). The Toggle is the classic checkbox (a white sunken square, a black tick when on). The Days are trackbar channels with a navy selection range; the Dial is a sunken groove with black ticks and the pointer thumb. On an exact pixel grid; its font (W95FA, SIL OFL 1.1) arrives with the theme fonts, Facet's draws it until then.",
